hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7104","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan from Iyad ibn Laqit al-Sadusi from Abu Rimthah who said: I went out with my father until we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw on his head traces of henna."
"7105","Haddathana Amr ibn al-Haytham Abu Qatan and Abu al-Nadr who said: Haddathana al-Masudi from Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The hand of the giver is the upper; your mother and your father and your sister and your brother, then the nearest, the nearest. And a man said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Yarbu, killers of so-and-so. He said: No soul shall commit a crime against another. And my father said: Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: I entered the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching and saying: The hand of the giver is the upper."
"7106","Haddathana Yunus, haddathana Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, haddathana Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while with him were people of Rabiah disputing over blood, and he said: The upper hand: your mother and your father and your sister and your brother, and the nearest, the nearest. He said: Then he looked and said: Who is this with you, Abu Rimthah. He said: I said: My son. He said: Indeed he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him. And he mentioned the story of the seal."
"7107","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Sufyan from Iyad ibn Laqit al-Sadusi who said: I heard Abu Rimthah al-Taymi who said: I came with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: This son of yours. I said: Yes. He said: Do you love him. I said: Yes. He said: Indeed he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him."
"7108","Haddathana Yunus, haddathana Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah from Asim from Abu Rimthah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while with him were people of Rabiah disputing over intentional blood, and I heard him say: Your mother and your father and your sister and your brother, then the nearest, the nearest. Then he said: Then he looked, then he said: Who is this with you, Abu Rimthah. So I said: My son. He said: Indeed he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him. He said: Then I looked, and in the cartilage of his shoulder was like a camel dropping or a pigeon egg, so I said: Shall I not treat you for it, O Messenger of Allah, for we are a household who practice medicine. So he said: He who placed it shall treat it."
"7109","Haddathana Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik and Affan who said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad, haddathana Iyad from Abu Rimthah who said: I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I saw him my father said to me: Do you know who this is. I said: No. So my father said to me: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I shuddered when he said that, and I had thought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was something unlike people, and behold a man with a wafrah. Affan said in his hadith: With a wafrah, and in it traces of henna, wearing two green garments. So my father greeted him, then we sat and talked for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: This son of yours. He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: Truly. He said: I testify to it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled laughing at the affirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father swearing over me. Then he said: Indeed he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: No bearer shall bear the burden of another. He said: Then he looked at what was like a lump between his shoulders and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am the most skilled of men; shall I not treat it for you. He said: No, its physician is He who created it."
"7110","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathana Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, haddathana Husayn ibn Ali from Ibn Abjar from Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah who said: I set out with my father while I was a boy to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So my father said to him: I am a physician, so show me this lump on your back. He said: And what will you do with it. He said: I will cut it off. He said: You are not a physician, but you are a companion; its physician is He who placed it. And another said: He who created it."
"7111","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathana Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman, haddathana Abu Awanah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Iyad ibn Laqit al-Ijli from Abu Rimthah al-Taymi of Taym al-Ribab who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my son, and he showed him to me, and I said to my son: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So trembling seized him in awe of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said to him: O Prophet of Allah, I am a physician of a household of physicians, so show me your back; if it is a lump I will lance it, and if it is other than that I will tell you, for there is no man more knowledgeable of a wound or an abscess than I. He said: Its physician is Allah. And upon him were two green cloaks; he had hair whiteness had overcome, and his gray was red. So he said: This son of yours. I said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: Your own son. I said: I testify to it. He said: Then he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him."
"7112","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathani Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, haddathana Muhammad ibn Bishr from Ali ibn Salih, haddathani Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah who said: I performed Hajj and saw a man sitting in the shade of the Kabah, so my father said: Do you know who this is; this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So when we reached him, behold a man with a wafrah with traces on it, and upon him two green garments."
"7113","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathani Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Naqid, haddathana Hushaym more than once who said: Akhbarani Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah al-Taymi: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of mine, and he said: This son of yours. I said: I testify to it. He said: He shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him. He said: And I saw the gray red."
"7114","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathani Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah, haddathana Yazid meaning Ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, haddathana Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran from a man, he is Thabit ibn Munqidh, from Abu Rimthah who said: I set out I and my father to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we were partway we met him, so my father said to me: O my son, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And I had thought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not resemble people, and behold a man with a wafrah with traces of henna on it, upon him two green cloaks. He said: As if I look at his shins. He said: So he said to my father: Who is this with you. He said: This, by Allah, is my son. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at my father swearing over me, then he said: You have spoken truth; indeed you shall not commit a crime against him nor shall he commit a crime against you. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: No bearer shall bear the burden of another."
"7115","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathana Muhammad ibn Bakkar, haddathana Qays ibn al-Rabi al-Asadi from Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah who said: I set out with my father while I was a boy, and we came to a man at midday sitting in the shade of his house, upon him two green cloaks, and his hair a wafrah, and on his head traces of henna. He said: So my father said to me: Do you know who this is. So I said: No. He said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So we talked long. He said: So my father said to him: I am a man of a household of medicine, so show me what is on the inside of your shoulder; if it is a lump I will cut it, and if it is other than that I will tell you. He said: Its physician is He who created it. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at me and said to him: This son of yours. He said: I testify to it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Look at what you say. He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at my resemblance to my father and at my father swearing over me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O man, he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him."
"7116","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathani Jafar ibn Humayd al-Kufi, haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit from his father from Abu Rimthah who said: I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I saw him my father said: Do you know who this is. I said: No. He said: This is Muhammad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I shuddered when he said that, and I had thought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was something unlike people, and behold a man with a wafrah and in it traces of henna, and upon him two green cloaks. So my father greeted him, then we sat and talked for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: This son of yours. He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: Truly. He said: I testify to it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled laughing at the affirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father swearing over me. Then he said: Indeed he shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: No bearer shall bear the burden of another. Then he looked at what was like a lump between his shoulders and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am as the most skilled of men; shall I not treat it for you. He said: No, its physician is He who created it."
"7117","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathani my father and Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb who said: Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit from his father from Abu Rimthah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while upon him were two green cloaks."
"7118","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathani Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah, haddathana Jarir meaning Ibn Hazim, haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Iyad ibn Laqit from Abu Rimthah who said: I came to Madinah and I had not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came out with two green garments upon him. So I said to my son: This, by Allah, is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So my son began trembling in awe of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a physician, and my father was a physician, and we are a household of medicine; by Allah nothing of the body is hidden from us, neither vein nor bone. So show me this on your shoulder; if it is a lump I will cut it then treat it. He said: No, its physician is Allah. Then he said: Who is this with you. I said: My son, by the Lord of the Kabah. So he said: Your son. He said: My son, I testify to it. He said: This son of yours shall not commit a crime against you nor shall you commit a crime against him."
